*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*% Open-source driver for the Polono PL70e-BT thermal label printer.
*% Not made, endorsed or supported by Polono. MIT licence, see LICENSE.
*% Generated by ppd/make_beeprt_ppds.py: edit that, not this file.
*% Option keywords and size names match Polono's own PPD on purpose, so
*% printers switched over from Polono's driver keep their saved settings.
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.0.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*PCFileName: "PL70EOPN.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "Polono"
*Product: "(PL70e-BT)"
*Product: "(ShippingPrinter PL70e-BT)"
*ModelName: "Polono PL70e-BT"
*ShortNickName: "Polono PL70e-BT (open-source)"
*NickName: "Polono PL70e-BT (open-source driver)"
*% The USB device ID is a best guess: it has not been seen on a real printer.
*1284DeviceID: "MFG:ShippingPrinter;MDL:PL70e-BT;CMD:TSPL;"
*PolonoProfile: "PL70e"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: False
*DefaultColorSpace: Gray
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*LandscapeOrientation: Minus90
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*cupsVersion: 1.5
*% macOS makes the copies: the printer gets each label as its own page.
*cupsManualCopies: True
*cupsFilter: "application/vnd.cups-raster 100 rastertotspl"

*% 4.08 in (104 mm) maximum width, 78.75 in maximum length.
*MaxMediaWidth: "294"
*MaxMediaHeight: "5670"
*HWMargins: 0 0 0 0
*CustomPageSize True: "pop pop pop <</PageSize[5 -2 roll]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*ParamCustomPageSize Width: 1 points 36 294
*ParamCustomPageSize Height: 2 points 36 5670
*ParamCustomPageSize WidthOffset: 3 points 0 0
*ParamCustomPageSize HeightOffset: 4 points 0 0
*ParamCustomPageSize Orientation: 5 int 0 0
*RequiresPageRegion All: True

*OpenGroup: General/General

